from pathlib import Path
import html,json
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;d=json.loads((R/'RESULTS.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'));precision=json.loads((R/'FAMILY-PRECISION.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
e=lambda x:html.escape(str(x))
def table(head,rows):return '<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr>'+''.join('<th>'+e(x)+'</th>' for x in head)+'</tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+str(x)+'</td>' for x in row)+'</tr>' for row in rows)+'</tbody></table></div>'
def label(p):return p['section']+' · hand '+p['hand']+' · '+p['variety']+' · '+p['format']
body='<p class="muted">VOYNICH · OPENING-ORDER AUDIT · v75</p><h1>Does sh- precede qok- across hands and readings?</h1><p class="notice">Source counts and within-line shuffles are shown separately from the broad opening-search correction. Finite-shuffle resolution can prevent the broad corrected screen from accepting even a very unusual target. Nonpassing under that limit is not evidence that order is absent.</p><p>H/F and every section, hand, Currier variety and raw format are kept separate. Primary raw P paragraphs only; all eligible folios included. The hand labelled “2, 3” remains ambiguous and cannot establish another known scribe. H/F are alternate readings of one manuscript.</p>'
body+='<h2>Principal relation · immediate readable neighbours</h2>'
rows=[]
for p in d['panels']:
 x=p['reported_rules'][0];a=precision[p['panel_index']];rows.append([e(label(p)),p['reading'],p['folios'],str(x['forward'])+' / '+str(x['reverse']),x['observed_D'],f'{x["null_mean"]:.2f}',e(x['null_95']),f'{x["p_raw_two_sided"]:.4f}',f'{x["p_search_family"]:.4f}',f'{x["p_all_panels"]:.4f}','At rank floor' if a['principal_at_best_possible_tail'] else 'Resolved rank'])
body+=table(['Stratum','Reading','Folios','sh→qok / reverse','Observed D','Null mean D','95% null range','Raw two-sided p','Opening-family p','All-panel p','Tail precision'],rows)
body+='<p>D is forward minus reverse. A positive count difference is an ordering preference, not an exception-free rule. Raw p-values are conditional on the line-shuffle null, before selecting opening pairs. No source lines or unknown slots are crossed.</p>'
body+='<h2>Search-family precision audit</h2><p>The declared family contains all one-, two- and three-character prefixes with at least 20 readable occurrences across at least two folios, plus every class needed for the four supplied comparisons regardless of support. Those support quantities are unchanged by within-line shuffles. All class pairs and both directions enter a pooled-rank minP correction. A further factor '+str(d['panel_count'])+' covers all H/F stratum panels.</p><p>With thousands of comparisons and only 5,000 calibration rows, many null comparisons can reach the smallest rank tail, 1/5000. The resulting minimum attainable family p is recorded below. A full-screen floor above .05 makes acceptance impossible in that calibration; such a failed screen is an inconclusive search-control limitation, not a decisive negative result. No extra shuffles or changed family were used to force acceptance.</p>'
body+=table(['Stratum','Reading','Opening pairs','Smallest attainable family p','Smallest attainable all-panel p','Forward null exceedances'],[[e(label(p)),p['reading'],p['class_pairs'],f'{a["minimum_achievable_family_p_in_this_calibration"]:.4f}',f'{a["minimum_achievable_all_panel_p"]:.4f}',a['principal_forward_null_exceedances']] for p,a in zip(d['panels'],precision)])
body+='<h2>What was reproduced—and what was not</h2><p>The quoted /tmp/claude-0/s/order.py was unavailable here and was not executed. Exact original category boundaries, adjacency handling and the approximately 60-pair search cannot be recovered from the pasted summary. The definitions and source handling here are explicit and frozen, rather than claimed to be a byte-for-byte reproduction.</p><p>sh-/qok-/d-/a- mean literal EVA prefixes; l/s means initial l OR s, including sh; ol/or means exact whole words ol and or. Types can overlap; no arbitrary exclusive classification is imposed. This is a new declared opening family, not the unknown original one.</p>'
if (R/'CLAIM-COMPARISON.json').exists():
 claims=json.loads((R/'CLAIM-COMPARISON.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
 body+=table(['Section','Claimed rule','Supplied H counts','Our pooled H counts','Exact count match'],[[e(x['section']),e(x['A']+' → '+x['B']),str(x['supplied_forward'])+'/'+str(x['supplied_reverse']),str(x['reconstructed_forward'])+'/'+str(x['reconstructed_reverse']),'yes' if x['exact_count_match'] else 'no: definitions/source handling unresolved'] for x in claims])
body+='<p>Definition ambiguity matters: “ol/or” could mean openings rather than exact words, and a mutually exclusive l/s class could exclude sh. A <a href="ALTERNATIVE-DEFINITION-AUDIT.json">separate postinspection raw-count audit</a> records those alternatives without replacing or rescoring the frozen primary tests. Neither alternative is asserted to recover the absent script.</p>'
body+='<details><summary>Section-pooled reproduction counts · audit only</summary><p>All source raw P lines, with hands and varieties pooled only to check the quoted totals. These are not the inferential panels above and cannot establish cross-scribe generalization.</p>'+table(['Section','Reading','Rule','Forward','Reverse'],[[e(p['section']),p['reading'],e(x['A']+' → '+x['B']),x['forward'],x['reverse']] for p in d['pooled_reproduction_audit'] for x in p['rules']])+'</details>'
body+='<h2>Other quoted relations · every stratum retained</h2>'
for p in d['panels']:
 body+='<details><summary>'+e(label(p))+' · '+p['reading']+'</summary>'+table(['A → B','Forward / reverse','D','Null mean','Raw p','Family p','All-panel p'],[[e(x['A']+' → '+x['B']),str(x['forward'])+'/'+str(x['reverse']),x['observed_D'],f'{x["null_mean"]:.2f}',f'{x["p_raw_two_sided"]:.4f}',f'{x["p_search_family"]:.4f}',f'{x["p_all_panels"]:.4f}'] for x in p['reported_rules']])+'<p>Word classes: '+str(len(p['labels']))+'; readable adjacent slots: '+str(p['mobility']['readable_adjacent_slots'])+'; movable word slots: '+str(p['mobility']['movable_word_slots'])+'.</p></details>'
body+='<h2>Folio support and reverse-order exceptions</h2><p>Each panel retains every principal-rule event, including all reverse pairs and zero/negative folios. These reversals contradict an exception-free sh-before-qok rule. They do not by themselves refute a probabilistic preference.</p>'
for p,s in zip(d['panels'],d['source_events']):
 body+='<details><summary>'+e(label(p))+' · '+p['reading']+' · '+str(len(s['events']))+' source events</summary>'+table(['Folio','Forward','Reverse','D'],[[e(f),v['forward'],v['reverse'],v['forward']-v['reverse']] for f,v in s['folios'].items()])
 for orient in ['reverse','forward']:
  body+='<details><summary>All '+orient+' passages</summary>'
  for ev in [ev for ev in s['events'] if ev['orientation']==orient]:
   i=ev['ordinal']-1;body+='<article><p><strong>'+e(ev['locator'])+'</strong> · first-word ordinal '+str(ev['ordinal'])+'</p><p class="raw">'+' '.join('□' if w is None else '<mark>'+e(w)+'</mark>' if j in (i,i+1) else e(w) for j,w in enumerate(ev['tokens']))+'</p></article>'
  body+='</details>'
 body+='</details>'
body+='<h2>Interpretive boundary</h2><p>Within-line shuffles preserve word frequency, each line’s words, first/last tokens and uncertainty barriers. They do not preserve every exact interior ordinal or all possible local spelling/junction constraints. Similar common final y does not make two boundary distributions identical, so it cannot alone rule out every boundary mechanism.</p><p>An ordering preference across multiple independently identified hands would be evidence of reusable written structure. It would not establish a specific grammar, a language, a semantic operation or a first result across this entire project. “z above 3” is not the conditional shuffle test used here, and multiple testing is not the only issue with independent-edge z assumptions.</p><p><a href="RESULTS.json">All panels and exceptions</a> · <a href="PROTOCOL.json">Frozen definitions</a> · <a href="FREEZE.json">Input/method hashes</a> · <a href="FAMILY-PRECISION.json">Search-resolution audit</a> · <a href="NON-P-FORMAT-INVENTORY.json">Separate non-P format inventory</a> · <a href="CLAIM-COMPARISON.json">Supplied-count audit</a> · <a href="VERIFICATION.json">Verification limits</a></p><p>Browser visual review not performed; source counts and numerical verification recorded separately.</p>'
css='''<style>:root{color-scheme:light dark;--bg:light-dark(#f5f2e9,#18251f);--fg:light-dark(#203f35,#e2e9df);--sub:light-dark(#54695b,#b4c7b7);--rule:light-dark(#c0ccbd,#48604d);--fill:light-dark(#e5ebda,#2a3e2d);--mark:light-dark(#e6edb7,#526330)}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--fg);font:16px/1.55 system-ui}main{max-width:1450px;padding:30px;margin:auto}h1{font-size:32px;line-height:1.2}h2{font-size:23px;margin-top:30px}p{max-width:1100px}a{color:inherit}.muted{color:var(--sub)}.notice{padding:16px;background:var(--fill)}.scroll{overflow-x:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}th,td{text-align:left;vertical-align:top;padding:9px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)}.raw{font:15px/1.8 ui-monospace,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere}mark{background:var(--mark);color:inherit}article{border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)}summary{cursor:pointer}details{margin:16px 0}@media(max-width:700px){main{padding:16px}}</style>'''
(R/'report.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Opening order across hands · v75</title>'+css+'</head><body><main>'+body+'</main></body></html>',encoding='utf-8');print('Opening-order report written with precision limits and reverse examples.')
